        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hawthornden Castle, Roslin Castle, Wallace's Cave, Roslin, Edinburgh, Rosslyn Chapel\n- Concepts: location, proximity, alternate names\n\nFacts:\n- Roslin Castle is located around 9 miles south of Edinburgh on the north bank of the North Esk.\n- Roslin Castle is only a few hundred metres from Rosslyn Chapel.\n- Hawthornden Castle lies one mile east of Roslin at grid reference NT287637.\n- Hawthornden Castle is just downstream from Roslin Castle.\n- Wallace's Cave is also known as Hawthornden Castle Cave.\n- Wallace's Cave is named after nearby Hawthornden Castle.",
